  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think it would be a great benefit to the map makers (and the vrchat population as well) if it would be possible to roll out a few simple scripts that could keep track of variables and manipulating said variables (Something like a calculator). This would in turn allow the possibility of adding health or calculating damage to an object depending on some type of weakness or strength. Also possibly add some simple AI script, like a usable path finding algorithm, that people could use in order to make worlds have enemies that attack you. This would greatly benefit a world such as SAO redux world and would vastly improve immersion and enjoyment.  Anything that would can be easily added to the current roster of the currently available vrchat scripts would be helpful. I only call for this because I have no clue when the play maker implementation is going to come out so an idea like this might be helpful for the short term to keep the game fresh.",
